WEBVTT


00:00:10.199 --> 00:00:11.849
BONNIE: (AS SANTA WOODY)
Ho, ho, howdy everyone.


00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.089
That sure was a fun Christmas.
(CRUNCHING)


00:00:15.199 --> 00:00:17.361
Hello, villagers. Whoo!


00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.448
Excuse me, pardon me, thank you.


00:00:19.559 --> 00:00:21.004
Hey, there, Baby Reindeer.


00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.599
Let's spread some Christmas cheer.


00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.125
(AS TRIXIE) I am the goblin fairy.


00:00:25.239 --> 00:00:28.164
I'll make you the most beautiful of all.
Pling!


00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.280
(AS JESSIE) Hooray!


00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:30.327
(AS TRIXIE) Excuse me, miss.


00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.363
There's a bug in my son's ice cream,
and he has a bug allergy.


00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:35.649
There you go, sweetheart. Enjoy.


00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:38.481
Oh, no! My dinosaur has escaped.


00:00:38.799 --> 00:00:39.960
I'll find you.


00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.167
- Did you hear that, Rex?
- I am a bit concerned.


00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.887
No! For once, I'm finally going to
get played with as a dinosaur.


00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.844
- Oh!
- Prepare yourself. Inhabit the part.


00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.725
You must not play the dinosaur,
you must be the dinosaur.


00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.569
But I am the dinosaur.


00:00:55.679 --> 00:00:59.365
Exactly! Now get out there and sparkle.


00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
(GASPS)


00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:03.439
There she is.


00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.450
The terrifying Kittysaurus.


00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.006
Oh, no. She laid millions of eggs.


00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.120
Ploop, ploop, ploop.


00:01:10.239 --> 00:01:11.240
(ROARS)


00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:13.680
BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie.
Get ready to leave, okay, sweetie?


00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:15.847
Coming! To be continued.


00:01:18.359 --> 00:01:19.805
Whoo! That was fun.


00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.001
The way Bonnie's mind works
is a mystery of science.


00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:23.804
- You make a fantastic little dinosaur.
- Well done, Kitty.


00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.763
- I was completely convinced.
- I didn't know you had it in you.


00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:27.325
- MR. PRICKLEPANTS: Bravo.
- (TRIXIE CLEARS THROAT)


00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:28.930
Oh! And, um, your portrayal of


00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:32.088
the disgruntled lunch counter patron
was gripping.


00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.368
Oh, don't worry, Trixie.
Next time you'll be a dinosaur for sure.


00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:38.210
Andy used to play with me
like a dinosaur all the time.


00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:40.280
Yeah, me too.
It's not all it's cracked up to be.


00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:42.045
- How would I know?
- Good point.


00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.447
BONNIE'S MOM: Honey, why don't you
bring some toys to share with Mason?


00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.846
I'll get my spaceship.


00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.723
Santa Woody, Villager,


00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.527
Daddy Reindeer, Baby Reindeer
and the terrifying Kittysaurus!


00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.164
- (ZIPPER CLOSES)
- (SIGHS)


00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.680
Greet the world with an open heart.


00:01:56.799 --> 00:01:57.840
(TRIXIE GROANS IN DISGUST)


00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.200
BONNIE'S MOM: Remember
to be polite, now.


00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.969
Please and thank you.


00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:02.760
MASON'S DAD: Hey!
Go on upstairs, Bonnie.


00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:03.921
Mason's easy to find.


00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.120
Mason!


00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:08.360
Mason?


00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:11.409
(VIDEO GAME SOUNDS)


00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.122
MASON: Whoa! Oh, duck.
Whoa, that was close!


00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.240
BONNIE: Um...


00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:16.560
(GASPS) You've got to be kidding me.


00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.681
He got an Optimum X for Christmas.


00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.927
- I never knew Mason liked video games.
- No! What?


00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:24.442
Sadly, the controls are
beyond my limitations.


00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.042
Limitations are the shackles
we bind to ourselves.


00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.006
Mason!


00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:32.242
Oh. Hey, Bonnie. Whoa!


00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.009
You have got to check this out.


00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:35.599
- Come on.
- Oh.


00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:36.879
Okay.


00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:39.689
(ALL SCREAMING)


00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.560
BUZZ: Mayday! Mayday!
TRIXIE: We're going in!


00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.560
(ALL GRUNT)


00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.121
Everyone okay?


00:02:51.479 --> 00:02:53.599
REX: I guess we're not
getting played with, after all.


00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:56.449
Well, who could blame her?
No one could resist an Optimum X.


00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.800
Where is everybody?


00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.524
Where's Sock Ape
and the little wrestlers


00:02:59.639 --> 00:03:00.879
and the Eco Force gang?


00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.401
Looks like we've got all afternoon
to find our old friends.


00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.126
Or maybe some new ones.


00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.004
Wow. Mason really hit the jackpot
this Christmas.


00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.646
- Nobody's this good.
- We're gonna meet some new toys!


00:03:11.759 --> 00:03:13.679
I'm both excited and panic-stricken.


00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.479
(TRIXIE READING)


00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:19.127
I love it.


00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.679
- (SNARLING)
- TRIXIE: Oh!


00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:20.725
- (SNARLING)
- TRIXIE: Oh!


00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:21.841
Hey!


00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:25.448
Oh! (GIGGLES)


00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.402
Here, boy. Here, little guy.


00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.926
- Trixie!
- Come on, gang. Let's stay together.


00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.930
TRIXIE: Hey. Slow down, buddy.
BUZZ: Where are you going?


00:03:34.039 --> 00:03:35.689
WOODY: Trixie!
REX: Hey! Trixie!


00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.164
(ANGEL KITTY PANTING)


00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:39.680
(MAKES LIZARD CLICK SOUNDS)


00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:40.800
(GASPS)


00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.444
You guys, this play date
just got very interesting.


00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.325
A complete set, fresh out of the box.


00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:52.168
- Where is everybody?
- Hello?


00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.441
(ALARM BLARING)


00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.882
Hey. Motion-activated room sentry.
Impressive.


00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.687
(YELLING)


00:04:01.039 --> 00:04:05.204
Whoa! Look at 'em.
They're like dinosaurs plus.


00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:08.004
With the Armour,
and the little red spears.


00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.639
- (GROWLING AND SNARLING)
- (CHUCKLES) Easy there, little doggy.


00:04:10.759 --> 00:04:12.045
(DINO-HOUND PURRING)


00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:15.800
Speak swiftly, foolish outlanders,
or suffer my battle blade.


00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.764
Ooh. (CLEARS THROAT)


00:04:17.879 --> 00:04:20.042
We are savage warriors,


00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.050
eager to slake our endless thirst
for conquest.


00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:25.964
(RAPTOR GUARDS MUMBLE)


00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.040
Ooh, nice.


00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.963
Everyone's so committed to their roles.


00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.564
REPTILLUS: Who goes there?


00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.680
(GRUNTS)


00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.800
Go talk to him, Sheriff.


00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.000
Uh, well, hi there, sir.


00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.441
My name is Woody and uh...
Nobody cares.


00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.562
What fearsome dinosaurs are these?


00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.091
- Oh.
- Oh.


00:04:46.199 --> 00:04:48.567
Greetings. I am Reptillus Maximus.


00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.250
And I am...


00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.725
Um...


00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.887
My name's Trixie. It's Trixie.


00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.605
You're not like our females.


00:04:57.159 --> 00:04:58.161
(SHRIEKS)


00:04:58.279 --> 00:05:01.124
Oh, you're quite
a unique specimen yourself.


00:05:01.519 --> 00:05:03.487
- (CHUCKLES)
- (HORN BLOWING)


00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.680
(CREAKING)


00:05:09.879 --> 00:05:11.165
(CHITTERING)


00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.810
Now we know
where they keep the fossils.


00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.079
- (CHUCKLES)
- (CLEARS THROAT)


00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.925
Strangers.
From the unforgiving outlands.


00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:23.363
We have travelled far.
From the distant Bonnie tribe.


00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.322
- (STIFLED LAUGHTER)
- Shh!


00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.451
- Hmm.
- (GRUNTS)


00:05:28.959 --> 00:05:31.769
- Leave your offerings and be gone.
- (REPTILLUS CLEARS THROAT)


00:05:31.879 --> 00:05:35.441
Are dinosaurs not welcome
in our great city, wise Cleric?


00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.848
(GROANS) Fine, fine.
Have them made presentable.


00:05:38.959 --> 00:05:42.009
I find their lack of Armour disturbing.


00:05:42.399 --> 00:05:44.004
(CHUCKLES) To the armoury!


00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.569
- Well, I think I'm going to head back.
- I'll go with you.


00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.720
I've had enough Shakespeare
in the park for one day.


00:05:49.959 --> 00:05:51.529
Suit yourself. See you later.


00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:52.641
(MUFFLED GRUNT)


00:05:52.759 --> 00:05:53.886
(CHUCKLING)


00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.081
Welcome to Battleopolis.


00:05:56.199 --> 00:05:57.406
(LAUGHS MENACINGLY)


00:06:01.399 --> 00:06:02.480
Oh, that's nice.


00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.170
Excellent. A nudge here, a jog there.


00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.007
Now go and be magnificent.


00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:12.247
Ray-Gon. Indulge this
dinosaur goddess in your finest wear.


00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.930
Mmm, I like where this is going.


00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.529
Oh, look at you.


00:06:15.639 --> 00:06:18.644
A ponderous monolithic canvas
to be adorned.


00:06:18.759 --> 00:06:19.759
Keep talking.


00:06:19.839 --> 00:06:23.286
The symmetry of a ceratopsid
and such strong anterior protuberi.


00:06:23.399 --> 00:06:24.447
You are so discerning.


00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.005
Oh, yes. I'm quite expert
in the enhancitizing


00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.521
and accoutramization
of Battlesaurs large and small.


00:06:32.879 --> 00:06:33.879
(GASPS)


00:06:35.439 --> 00:06:36.441
Ooh!


00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.324
- Okay, I'll take that.
- Oh, yes, of course.


00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:39.805
TRIXIE: And that.
RAY-GON: Plasma core warheads.


00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:40.887
TRIXIE: Well, you never know.


00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.286
RAY-GON: Gauntlets.
TRIXIE: Check. Very nice.


00:06:42.399 --> 00:06:43.639
RAY-GON: Dorsal sensoid plates.


00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.130
TRIXIE: For me?
RAY-GON: Oh, most certainly.


00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.685
Do you have the battle gogs in "flame"?


00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.959
- Do you have to ask?
- Dish 'em on over, little fella.


00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:51.447
Have I mentioned
what a fantastic time I'm having?


00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.846
It is as plain as the horn on your face.


00:06:53.959 --> 00:06:55.485
- (GIGGLES)
- (CHUCKLES)


00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.204
Uh, when do I get a turn?


00:06:57.319 --> 00:06:59.367
(LAUGHS) I haven't
forgotten you, brother.


00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.480
TRIXIE: It's perfect!


00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.480
(CLEARS THROAT)


00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.040
- (REPTILLUS CHUCKLES)
- Ready for me?


00:07:04.439 --> 00:07:06.204
- (INDISTINCT WHISPERS)
- (RAY-GON SHUDDERS)


00:07:06.319 --> 00:07:07.889
Well? What do you think?


00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.641
The Elders shall gaze
upon this Battlesaur


00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:13.047
with full and rapturous pride.


00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.208
That's exactly what I thought you'd say.


00:07:15.319 --> 00:07:16.319
REX: Hey, Trixie.


00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.167
Trixie! Ha!
Who's a fierce dinosaur now? (ROARS)


00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:21.850
The Ultimate Dinosaurs.


00:07:21.959 --> 00:07:24.565
(CHUCKLES) Come.
Battleopolis awaits.


00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.288
This set is incredible.


00:07:29.439 --> 00:07:30.771
I could really get used to this.


00:07:30.879 --> 00:07:33.201
- Give us some muscle.
- You're a bruiser, aren't ya, lad?


00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.331
Prehistoric buildings, dinosaur cars,


00:07:36.439 --> 00:07:38.886
whatever that thing's meant to be.
What is it?


00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.127
The Triassic Tower of the Dream Elders


00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.481
through which distant beings


00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.841
convey cosmic wisdom
from another dimension.


00:07:45.959 --> 00:07:49.247
Ah, at our house, Bonnie just yells
across the room in a funny voice.


00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.441
(THE CLERIC GROANS)


00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.769
And here, the Volcano Command Base.
My domain.


00:07:53.879 --> 00:07:56.610
Everyone needs an apartment
shaped like their own head.


00:07:58.279 --> 00:07:59.610
Battle well, brother.


00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.130
With strength and honour.


00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.240
(GRUNTS)


00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.331
Pricklepants is right.


00:08:05.439 --> 00:08:07.487
You just need to be the Battlesaur.


00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.762
Your Prickly-pants is a wise prophet.


00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:12.288
Battle is everything to us.


00:08:12.399 --> 00:08:13.605
Our survival.


00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.209
Our legacy.


00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.000
From a kingdom long ago.


00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.884
♪ An enigma wrapped in mystery


00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.651
♪ We've battled every foe


00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:27.002
♪ Since before the dawn of history


00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.451
♪ History


00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.608
♪ Battlesaurs Battlesaurs


00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.130
♪ Battlesaurs ♪


00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.525
(ALL CHEERING)


00:08:33.919 --> 00:08:35.808
(CHUCKLES) You even have
a theme song?


00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.600
(SIGHS) You seem to have everything.


00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.370
(CHUCKLES) You are a puzzle, Trixie.


00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.051
Well, technically,
I'm a poseable action figure.


00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:46.249
(CHUCKLES) Now tell me
more of your world.


00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.600
Oh, it's nothing like this.


00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.322
I'll bet you have
the most amazing play times.


00:08:52.679 --> 00:08:54.250
Play times?


00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.331
I do not understand.


00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.442
Oh, you know, play.


00:08:58.559 --> 00:09:01.529
When you give yourself over to a kid.


00:09:01.639 --> 00:09:03.289
Giving is surrender.


00:09:03.399 --> 00:09:05.481
A Battlesaur would never surrender.


00:09:06.399 --> 00:09:07.399
Ooh.


00:09:08.279 --> 00:09:09.485
So serious.


00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.725
(CHUCKLES)


00:09:11.759 --> 00:09:16.368
Trixie, you cause me
to question all that I know.


00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.527
(GROWLS)


00:09:17.639 --> 00:09:18.119
(BEEPING)


00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.006
(BEEPING)


00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.090
Time for battle! Time for battle!


00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.368
- Time for battle! Time for battle!
- (BATTLESAURS YELL)


00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:25.480
Oh, what's that?


00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.240
The great Dream Elder beckons us,
to the Arena of Woe.


00:09:29.759 --> 00:09:30.841
Okay.


00:09:38.879 --> 00:09:40.005
(ALL CHEERING)


00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.769
BATTLESAURS: Reptillus! Reptillus!


00:09:41.879 --> 00:09:43.290
BATTLESAUR: Yay, love you!


00:09:44.679 --> 00:09:45.966
(CHEERING)


00:09:48.519 --> 00:09:49.519
(GASPS)


00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:52.639
(ROARS)


00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:54.130
(CHEERING UPROARIOUSLY)


00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.240
(GIGGLING)


00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.840
(ROARING)


00:09:58.759 --> 00:10:00.409
Well, this seems festive.


00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.203
(CREAKING)


00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:11.080
Let the battle begin.


00:10:11.399 --> 00:10:12.764
(HORN BLOWING)


00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:15.801
RAPTOR GUARD: Get on up there.


00:10:15.919 --> 00:10:18.399
Sock Ape! Pengo! Fauntleroy!


00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:23.086
Oh, this'll be good. I'll do a jab,
then you pretend to attack me, then...


00:10:23.639 --> 00:10:25.129
You guys are so jumpy.


00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:26.365
(SHOUTING)


00:10:28.279 --> 00:10:29.280
- (CHEERING)
- Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!


00:10:29.399 --> 00:10:31.049
Why are you doing this?


00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:36.360
- (WHIMPERS)
- (GRUNTS)


00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.889
(ALL CLAMOURING)


00:10:40.559 --> 00:10:42.687
It's doomsday.


00:10:42.919 --> 00:10:43.919
(GROWLS)


00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:46.640
(RIPPING)


00:10:47.919 --> 00:10:48.919
TRIXIE: Hey!


00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.286
(DINO-HOUNDS SNARLING)


00:10:53.879 --> 00:10:54.879
- Trixie?
- Trixie?


00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.008
- What?
- Trixie, the Battlesaurs are not playing.


00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.168
They've never been played with.
They don't even know they're toys!


00:11:00.279 --> 00:11:01.519
Incredible, isn't it?


00:11:01.639 --> 00:11:02.879
(SINISTER CHUCKLE)


00:11:05.559 --> 00:11:06.559
(REPTILLUS YELLING)


00:11:12.519 --> 00:11:13.725
(GASPS) No!


00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.167
You got a crayon?


00:11:16.919 --> 00:11:17.919
(YELLING)


00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.000
(LOW GROWL)


00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:26.765
(GROWLS ANGRILY)


00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.759
BUZZ: Buzz-Buzz-Buzz Lightyear
to the rescue!


00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.480
Blast.


00:11:56.879 --> 00:11:58.529
- (DINO-HOUNDS SNARLING)
- (GRUNTING)


00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:00.284
- Back off, you...
- What?


00:12:00.399 --> 00:12:01.561
You bully!


00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:06.448
Curse! Release the Goliathon.


00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:07.640
(CHEERING)


00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.240
(LAUGHING EVILLY)


00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:17.330
(ROARS)


00:12:23.919 --> 00:12:24.919
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:12:26.279 --> 00:12:27.441
(GRUNTING)


00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.200
Oh!


00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.720
(SLURPS)


00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:34.767
(CHEERING)


00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.203
Cough up my friends, you, you...


00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.650
(ALL GASPING)


00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.808
As I suspected.


00:12:47.919 --> 00:12:49.888
She bears the mark of obedience.


00:12:50.559 --> 00:12:52.448
What? This?


00:12:54.799 --> 00:12:55.880
I thought I knew you.


00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:58.364
I was thinking the same thing.


00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.807
She is an enemy to the tribe.


00:13:00.919 --> 00:13:03.525
Ray-Gon. The Supplicator.


00:13:03.639 --> 00:13:05.562
The Supplicator?
Hardly a suitable nomenclature.


00:13:05.679 --> 00:13:07.283
- I will not stand for this sort of abuse.
- (LAUGHS EVILLY)


00:13:07.399 --> 00:13:08.525
(YELLS)


00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.203
Rex, have you completely lost it?


00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.447
I'm sorry. I can't control myself.


00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:30.287
There is no escape,
Trixie of the Bonn-Ye tribe.


00:13:30.399 --> 00:13:31.970
(LAUGHS)


00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.565
(GASPS) Bonnie!


00:13:35.679 --> 00:13:37.364
- BUZZ: Run, Trixie!
- Get Bonnie!


00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.447
- (DINO-HOUNDS SNARLING)
- (GASPS)


00:13:46.799 --> 00:13:48.768
Reptillus. Stop her.


00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:01.721
(GRUNTS)


00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:04.480
Huh?


00:14:09.639 --> 00:14:10.639
What?


00:14:27.879 --> 00:14:28.879
(GRUNTS)


00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.440
(CHUCKLES)


00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:40.605
(CHATTERING)


00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.768
Hmm! Robot. Obey.


00:14:42.879 --> 00:14:43.961
(STARTLED GRUNT)


00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.365
Oh! Ah! Oh!


00:14:46.679 --> 00:14:47.679
Ew!


00:14:50.919 --> 00:14:51.919
WOODY: Rex.
BUZZ: Rex.


00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.000
REX: I can't help it!


00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:54.561
(CHOKING)


00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.284
- Woody.
- What?


00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.363
Hey! Hey, that's Mason and Bonnie.


00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.051
Oh, I get it.
You're glad Mason got the Optimum X.


00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.321
He plays there.


00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:08.328
While I rule here.


00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.205
My Battlesaurs have no use for play.


00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:15.166
They have everything they need,
content in their ignorance.


00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.408
- What's ignorance?
- (GRUNTS)


00:15:17.519 --> 00:15:19.249
You've been a busy little tyrant.


00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.804
And only two days since Christmas.


00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.923
Ka-Rist-Maas?


00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.365
The joy that you give to others
is the joy that comes back to you.


00:15:27.759 --> 00:15:29.682
- Aw.
- (GRUNTS ANGRILY)


00:15:29.799 --> 00:15:33.282
- You will all be cast into the pit.
- Pit?


00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:34.399
"Pit?
"Pit?


00:15:34.759 --> 00:15:36.125
(LAUGHING EVILLY)


00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.280
(TRIXIE PANTING)


00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.445
I've got to shut it down.


00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:55.840
(SIGHS)


00:15:58.399 --> 00:15:59.400
(GRUNTS)


00:16:02.159 --> 00:16:05.049
- Come on, buddy. Fight it off.
- Rex, resist the Supplicator.


00:16:05.159 --> 00:16:06.490
Sorry. I'm sorry.


00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:13.840
Oh, boy.


00:16:19.639 --> 00:16:21.085
- No.
- (GASPS)


00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:22.840
(GASPS)


00:16:26.279 --> 00:16:27.279
(GROWLS)


00:16:28.399 --> 00:16:30.846
Reptillus.
Your world is bigger than you know.


00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:33.249
Let me show you who you really are.


00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.124
But I am a Battlesaur.


00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:38.482
You can be so much more.
And you know it.


00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:41.530
(THE CLERIC LAUGHS EVILLY)


00:16:41.919 --> 00:16:43.331
(RAPTOR GUARDS CHANTING)


00:16:45.799 --> 00:16:48.370
(PLAYING SOLEMN TUNE)


00:16:55.399 --> 00:16:56.480
Pipe down, you.


00:16:59.879 --> 00:17:03.326
Reptillus, it's your kid who chooses
what you're going to be.


00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.604
It could be a dinosaur,


00:17:05.759 --> 00:17:09.605
a baby reindeer
or something you'd never even think of.


00:17:10.759 --> 00:17:13.490
It's about being there for your kid.


00:17:13.759 --> 00:17:15.204
It's about...


00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.089
Surrender.


00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:24.161
Huh?


00:17:24.279 --> 00:17:27.328
- This bus is out of gas.
- Dang it, the power's down.


00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.961
Oh, hello. Are you lost?


00:17:45.599 --> 00:17:46.760
Come see my igloo.


00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.961
We can wait inside with the polar bears


00:17:49.079 --> 00:17:51.320
and the salamanders until they find us.


00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:52.601
Check the supplies.


00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.200
We have hamburgers,
pasgetti, pancakes,


00:17:55.319 --> 00:17:56.809
chocolate milk, gummy worms...


00:17:56.920 --> 00:18:00.845
- Oh, what planet is he from?
- Neptune! Or maybe Florida.


00:18:05.119 --> 00:18:06.609
(BUZZ AND WOODY GROANING)


00:18:09.279 --> 00:18:10.247
- (SCREAMING)
- Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!


00:18:10.359 --> 00:18:11.359
(LAUGHS)


00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.162
(BOTH LAUGHING AND WHOOPING)


00:18:17.279 --> 00:18:19.281
We crash-landed on the party planet.


00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.049
Aliens everywhere.


00:18:22.519 --> 00:18:24.521
Wait. Where's my baby reindeer?


00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.650
(GASPS) There she is.


00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.000
(WHISPERING)


00:18:30.119 --> 00:18:32.326
She says, "Put on your dance pants."


00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.050
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)


00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.689
Look, Buzz, I'm a boneless chicken.


00:18:41.119 --> 00:18:42.962
BONNIE: (AS TRIXIE)
How about a dance, Uncle Wormy?


00:18:43.079 --> 00:18:44.640
MASON: (AS THE CLERIC)
I don't know how.


00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:46.765
BONNIE: (GASPS) He's adorable.


00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:48.039
MASON: Boop! Boop! Beep! Bop!


00:18:48.079 --> 00:18:50.526
BONNIE: Come on, Mega-Monster,
let's fight some crime.


00:18:58.759 --> 00:19:00.364
(BONNIE AND MASON LAUGHING)


00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:04.086
That was glorious.


00:19:04.599 --> 00:19:06.682
It was, wasn't it?


00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.400
MASON'S DAD: It's always so great
to have Bonnie around.


00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:10.680
Let's have her back next week.


00:19:10.799 --> 00:19:14.009
BONNIE'S MOM: So, shall we say
Tuesday around 3:30?


00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.967
- BONNIE'S MOM: Bonnie!
- (MAKES AIRCRAFT LANDING SOUNDS)


00:19:23.079 --> 00:19:25.366
- Dinner, sweetie.
- Bye, toys.


00:19:26.279 --> 00:19:27.280
Whoo-hoo!


00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:29.810
So, how was the play date?


00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.843
Oh, you know, typical crash-landing.


00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:34.166
Hostile lizard people,
hand-to-hand combat.


00:19:34.279 --> 00:19:36.442
And I was a mindless,
lumbering automaton.


00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:38.847
- Well, that part adds up.
- What about you, Trixie?


00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.288
Have you finally found
a role that suits you?


00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.880
- Goblin fairy, ghost clown...
- Hey, hey! Easy now!


00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.569
...dancing queen, a baby reindeer.


00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:48.250
You name it. I'm Bonnie's dinosaur.


00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:52.042
And Bonnie's dinosaur
gets to be everything.


00:19:52.279 --> 00:19:54.123
Be grateful for your gifts.


00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.923
They are all around you.


00:19:56.039 --> 00:19:57.326
ALL: Aww.


00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.565
(SOCK APE SNORING)


00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:19.570
(THE CLERIC SIGHS)


00:20:25.799 --> 00:20:28.962
Farewell, Trixie
of the Bonn-Ye tribe.


00:20:29.359 --> 00:20:32.807
My heart will burn bright
at the moment of your return.


00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:35.800
Tuesday, around 3:30.
